steps.body:
Component scanning registers any class carrying a stereotype annotation:

- `@Component`: a generic bean.
- `@Service`: business logic. Behaves exactly like `@Component`; the name documents intent.
- `@Repository`: data access. Also translates persistence exceptions into Spring's `DataAccessException` family.
- `@Controller` / `@RestController`: the web layer.

```java
@Service
public class OrderService {
    private final PaymentClient payments;
    private final OrderRepository orders;

    public OrderService(PaymentClient payments, OrderRepository orders) {
        this.payments = payments;
        this.orders = orders;
    }
}
```

With a **single constructor**, Spring uses it automatically: no `@Autowired` needed. It injects by **type**, so asking for the interface `PaymentClient` is normal.

