    public OrderService(InvoiceService invoices) { ... }
}

@Service
public class InvoiceService {
    public InvoiceService(OrderService orders) { ... }
}
```

To build `OrderService`, Spring needs `InvoiceService`, which needs `OrderService`... With constructor injection there's no valid order, so startup fails with *The dependencies of some of the beans in the application context form a cycle*, plus a little diagram of the loop.

Since Spring Boot 2.6, cycles through field or setter injection are rejected by default too. The fix is design, not configuration: move the shared logic into a third bean, or decouple one direction with an application event.

```java
import org.springframework.web.bind.annotation.*;

@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/books")
public class BookController {

    private final BookService books;

    public BookController(BookService books) {
        this.books = books;
    }

    @GetMapping("/{id}")
    public BookResponse get(@PathVariable Long id) {
        return books.find(id);
    }
}
```

- `@RestController` = `@Controller` + `@ResponseBody`: return values are written to the response body (as JSON, via Jackson) instead of being treated as view names.
- `@RequestMapping` on the class sets a shared path prefix.
- `@GetMapping`, `@PostMapping`, `@PutMapping`, `@PatchMapping` and `@DeleteMapping` map one HTTP method plus a path.

```java
// GET /api/books/42
@GetMapping("/{id}")
public BookResponse get(@PathVariable Long id) { ... }

// GET /api/books?author=Herbert&page=2
@GetMapping
public List<BookResponse> search(@RequestParam String author,
                                 @RequestParam(defaultValue = "0") int page) { ... }

// POST /api/books with a JSON body
@PostMapping
public BookResponse create(@RequestBody CreateBookRequest request) { ... }
```

- `@PathVariable`: a path segment that identifies the resource.
- `@RequestParam`: a query-string parameter. **Required by default**, unless you give a `defaultValue` or `required = false`.
- `@RequestBody`: the JSON body, deserialized by Jackson.

